{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey Security Deposit Law","requirement":"A landlord may not collect a security deposit above one and one-half times one month's rent, must hold deposits in trust in an interest-bearing account and pay the tenant the interest, and must return the deposit plus interest less itemized deductions within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; yearly deposit increase max 10%","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental tenancies in New Jersey. The deposit-holding and account provisions do not apply to seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All residential rentals; deposit-account rules exempt seasonal rentals of 125 days or less"},"exemptions":"Seasonal use or rental for a term of not more than 125 consecutive days by a person whose permanent residence is elsewhere; seasonal, temporary or migrant farm worker housing is not within that seasonal exclusion.","penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees, if the deposit is not returned within 30 days.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19 et seq.","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act security deposit return after domestic-violence lease termination","requirement":"A tenant who terminates a lease under the Safe Housing Act is entitled to the security deposit; the landlord must make the deposit plus interest available within 15 business days after termination and give written notice of where and when to collect it within three business days.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease because the tenant or a child faces an imminent threat of serious physical harm from a named person; does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Domestic-violence lease terminations"},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
